<type>(<scope>)!: <summary>

# Why is this change needed? What problem does it solve? (wrap at 72 cols)

# Footer (optional):
# Closes #123
# BREAKING CHANGE: describe what breaks and how to migrate
#
# Types:
#   feat      new functionality (minor)
#   fix       bug fix (patch)
#   chore     maintenance, tooling
#   docs      documentation only
#   ci        CI/CD and automation
#   refactor  behavior-preserving code change
#   test      add or update tests
#   perf      performance improvement
#   build     build system or dependencies
#   style     formatting only, no logic change
#   revert    revert an earlier commit
#   ai        agent prompts, skills, AI config
#
# Rules:
#   - Subject: imperative mood ("add", not "added"), <= 72 chars, no trailing period
#   - Scope is optional: feat(parser): ...
#   - Add "!" after type/scope for a breaking change (major bump)
#   - Body explains WHY, not what; the diff shows what
#   - Never commit secrets; never use --no-verify
